WEBVTT

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:07.110
<i>It's about time you pay us 
back the money we lent you.</i>

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:07.100
<b>We'll bury you!</b>

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:07.100
<b>We'll drown you in trash                      Die</b>

00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:09.450
<i>We've got to have you do</i>

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:11.980
<i>whatever you can possibly do, Shirokane-san!</i>

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:14.660
<i>Endure it, Ginka, endure it.</i>

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:18.160
<i>I don't want this anymore...</i>

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:28.480
We worked really hard.

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:30.000
A-Akari-san...

00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:31.670
There's dirt...

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:34.260
Thanks.

00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:39.570
All right! Let's go back 
and eat ice cream!

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:41.520
Hey, young ladies.

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:47.150
Is the place called 
Sefiro Fiore up ahead?

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:48.570
Yes.

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:49.900
It is.

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:52.660
Thank goodness.

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:56.220
I kept walking and walking 
and the hill never ended.

00:00:56.220 --> 00:00:58.360
Not to mention, today's 
pretty humid, ain't it?

00:00:58.360 --> 00:00:59.540
And look at me.

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:04.440
I was about to give up and then 
I ran into you young ladies.

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:06.430
You two are angels!

00:01:07.510 --> 00:01:10.420
It wasn't that big of a deal.

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:13.170
Um, did you have something 
to do at Sefiro Fiore?

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:18.760
Oh, right! Sorry, I forgot 
to introduce myself. I'm—

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:21.180
Hey, Pops!

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:26.230
Who were you, again?

00:01:26.230 --> 00:01:27.990
What the hell?

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:31.230
A flying retort...

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:32.980
That was a nice retort, Ginka.

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:34.690
And that was a nice joke, Pops!

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:36.700
Are they family?

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:38.070
It appears so.

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:12.170
<b>Ah, Money, Money! 
How Many Sad Things Must Occur 
in This World Due to Money?</b>

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:12.170
Thank you, as always, Shirokane-san

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:15.130
for your very generous 
monthly donations.

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:18.670
Ain't nothing to it.

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:23.080
Ya'll Elemental Tarot users are 
the treasures of humanity.

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:26.430
You protect us and take care of the bad guys... Ba-ba-ba-ba-bam...

00:03:27.970 --> 00:03:30.680
You guys fight to protect 
humanity, just like that.

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:31.980
Right.

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:33.690
<i>It's gotten rather stuffy in here.</i>

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:38.640
When we were poor, we were 
always getting helped out by others,

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:41.070
so I'd like to return 
the favor a little.

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:44.260
To think that my kid 
ended up receiving

00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:46.490
the power that my aunt awakened to...

00:03:46.490 --> 00:03:47.830
She's...

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:50.330
She's the pride of our family.

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:53.250
Please keep taking care of her.

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:56.840
My pops is the president of 
a discount store chain.

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:58.840
You've heard of Sancho Panza, right?

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:00.840
The place where the sales 
floor is sort of a mess?

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:03.050
Yup. That's my pops' company.

00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:04.600
That's amazing!

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:07.680
That place has all sorts of 
things, so it's a lot of fun.

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:10.350
Ginka's room is a mess, too.

00:04:10.590 --> 00:04:13.200
That's an homage to my pops' store.

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:14.800
Ho-Homage?

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:17.990
Both me and my pops can't relax 
unless we're surrounded with stuff.

00:04:17.990 --> 00:04:21.360
We end up worrying about 
not being able to buy stuff again.

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:23.250
Not to mention, we used to be poor.

00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:26.380
He opened up a takoyaki shop, 
but it quickly went under.

00:04:26.380 --> 00:04:28.760
So, while we were running 
around with all this debt,

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:30.620
he got an idea and invented

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:33.870
a home takoyaki machine, 
and it was a hit.

00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:36.590
And that turned into 
the company he has now.

00:04:36.590 --> 00:04:37.760
Wow...

00:04:37.770 --> 00:04:41.380
There you are, my angels!

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:45.000
We're heading to a party right 
now. A party! Let's go!

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:55.350
Wow! It really is a party!

00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:58.800
Thought you might be 
sick of the cafeteria's food,

00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:00.860
so there are plenty of sweets, too.

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:03.190
Eat what you want and 
build up some stamina.

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:05.240
Chicken salad...

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:08.030
We've got to go greet 
some people, Ginka.

00:05:08.030 --> 00:05:10.670
Okay! See you guys later.

00:05:10.670 --> 00:05:11.950
Chicken salad...

00:05:14.920 --> 00:05:17.770
I-I can't really get used to this.

00:05:17.770 --> 00:05:20.880
Really? If you don't move, 
they'll leave you alone.

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:22.090
So it's pretty relaxing.

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:25.340
This isn't your first time, Luna-chan?

00:05:25.690 --> 00:05:30.390
No. We have a few parties 
at my house each year, too.

00:05:30.390 --> 00:05:31.470
But...

00:05:32.070 --> 00:05:37.100
I didn't have a father who'd 
escort me like Ginka-san.

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:39.480
A father, huh?

00:05:56.260 --> 00:05:58.980
Ginka-chan, you've grown!

00:05:58.980 --> 00:06:00.490
And you've gotten so pretty.

00:06:00.490 --> 00:06:05.010
Oh, it's probably because I'm 
using your company's toner.

00:06:05.010 --> 00:06:06.630
You should totally send me more.

00:06:08.120 --> 00:06:09.530
Oh, man...

00:06:09.530 --> 00:06:10.760
By the way, where's Honda?

00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:13.520
What? You haven't heard, Shirokane-san?

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:16.270
His company is about to go bankrupt.

00:06:16.490 --> 00:06:18.350
What?! Are you serious?

00:06:18.670 --> 00:06:21.360
I thought you knew, 
since you're friends.

00:06:21.750 --> 00:06:23.820
No, I had no idea.

00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:25.730
What happened to Uncle Honda?

00:06:26.030 --> 00:06:28.290
He's had some bad luck.

00:06:28.290 --> 00:06:30.500
Like a ship with 
his freight sinking,

00:06:30.500 --> 00:06:33.490
and not being able to sell the rest 
of his stock because he was a day late.

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:36.590
I heard he's been 
borrowing money from

00:06:36.590 --> 00:06:38.250
some dangerous places lately.

00:06:38.570 --> 00:06:41.320
I had no idea.

00:06:45.330 --> 00:06:48.520
So, what're you gonna do, Honda-san?

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:52.430
You've got two options, right?

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:58.490
In the end, it's up to you 
what you're gonna do, Honda-san.

00:07:05.200 --> 00:07:06.380
Well?

00:07:06.380 --> 00:07:08.260
It's no use. His phone's been cut.

00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:10.370
Why'd Uncle have to be like that?

00:07:10.370 --> 00:07:12.440
I wonder why he didn't tell us.

00:07:12.440 --> 00:07:15.370
He's always been self-conscious 
about weird things.

00:07:15.780 --> 00:07:19.120
Um, what kind of person is Honda-san?

00:07:19.730 --> 00:07:22.330
He's a classmate of mine from college.

00:07:23.320 --> 00:07:26.420
Honda was the heir to the famous 
trading conglomerate, La Poncho,

00:07:27.340 --> 00:07:29.520
and I was a poor student 
full of dreams.

00:07:29.970 --> 00:07:31.840
We came from totally
different backgrounds,

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:34.010
but we somehow clicked.

00:07:34.480 --> 00:07:36.210
He helped us out quite a bit

00:07:36.210 --> 00:07:39.980
when my takoyaki shop went 
under and we were poor.

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:43.600
I remember that well.

00:07:46.870 --> 00:07:49.090
<i>You okay, Ginka-chan?</i>

00:07:55.300 --> 00:07:56.330
<i>Ginka-chan.</i>

00:07:57.230 --> 00:07:58.330
<i>Uncle!</i>

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:04.760
<i>You okay?</i>

00:08:07.560 --> 00:08:09.140
<i>Here, I brought you a gift.</i>

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:14.030
He would always help me feel a lot 
better because he'd do things

00:08:14.660 --> 00:08:19.230
like bring me sweets while 
the loan sharks went away.

00:08:22.130 --> 00:08:23.360
Honda...

00:08:28.350 --> 00:08:30.530
Was there a worthy one at the party?

00:08:30.830 --> 00:08:34.780
Yes, though I don't know if 
he'll be to your liking or not.

00:08:35.440 --> 00:08:37.530
I'm sure he's fine if you picked him.

00:08:38.050 --> 00:08:40.040
Is that a compliment?

00:08:44.320 --> 00:08:48.020
Dress differently when 
you come here next.

00:08:48.560 --> 00:08:51.800
Why? You're the one who suggested this.

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:54.520
The people around me are 
becoming suspicious.

00:08:54.520 --> 00:08:56.900
I don't want to be caught 
up in some scandal.

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:25.080
That pig.

00:09:34.410 --> 00:09:36.590
It's no use. I can't concentrate.

00:09:38.290 --> 00:09:40.290
A dad, huh?

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:43.470
<i>What? So you've never asked?</i>

00:09:43.840 --> 00:09:45.620
<i>I asked once,</i>

00:09:45.620 --> 00:09:50.210
<i>but Mom looked really sad 
when I asked about my dad.</i>

00:09:50.630 --> 00:09:51.950
<i>I see...</i>

00:09:51.950 --> 00:09:56.790
<i>Well, he was never there, 
so I'm not really lonely.</i>

00:09:58.390 --> 00:10:00.870
<i>We're, well...</i>

00:10:01.390 --> 00:10:03.870
<i>Family already...</i>

00:10:04.880 --> 00:10:06.870
<i>Read this and cheer up, okay?</i>

00:10:14.140 --> 00:10:18.110
Fuyuna was more to me 
than a father ever...

00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:35.870
Yataro, Ginka-chan...

00:10:36.840 --> 00:10:41.840
I'm sorry. I fell out of 
the business god's grace.

00:10:46.800 --> 00:10:51.060
It was my dream to be at 
Ginka-chan's wedding.

00:10:54.390 --> 00:10:56.910
But everything's finished.

00:11:04.960 --> 00:11:06.390
Wait, Mister.

00:11:06.750 --> 00:11:10.140
You have money troubles, right?

00:11:10.970 --> 00:11:12.860
Want me to help you out?

00:11:14.120 --> 00:11:17.780
It'd be a waste to die over 
a hundred million or two.

00:11:18.150 --> 00:11:20.420
Who do you belong to?

00:11:20.420 --> 00:11:21.530
What are you talking about?

00:11:33.200 --> 00:11:36.980
People can do anything once 
they're ready to die, right?

00:11:39.400 --> 00:11:42.050
Yeah, you're right.

00:11:42.780 --> 00:11:45.680
I'll grant your wish.

00:12:03.300 --> 00:12:04.620
You serious, Pops?

00:12:04.620 --> 00:12:06.740
Uncle's company recovered?

00:12:06.740 --> 00:12:08.450
<b>Sancho Panza</b>

00:12:06.740 --> 00:12:08.450
Serious! Totally serious!

00:12:08.450 --> 00:12:10.410
It's a miracle! A miracle!

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:11.890
<i>But how?</i>

00:12:12.940 --> 00:12:15.020
Well, I'm not sure how, but apparently

00:12:15.020 --> 00:12:17.940
his debt suddenly disappeared.

00:12:17.940 --> 00:12:20.630
The world's sure full 
of mysteries, isn't it?

00:12:20.630 --> 00:12:23.930
Who cares as long as 
Uncle Honda is okay!

00:12:23.930 --> 00:12:24.980
<i>You're right.</i>

00:12:24.980 --> 00:12:29.010
<i>I also heard that Honda's happily 
working because of that.</i>

00:12:29.010 --> 00:12:30.820
That's really great!

00:12:30.820 --> 00:12:31.600
<i>That's poncho great, 
since it's La Poncho.</i>

00:12:31.600 --> 00:12:32.770
That's poncho great, 
since it's La Poncho. {M: I don't even know how to work in poncho to mean great as a pun... maybe it'll come to me later :/ if anyone has any ideas, feel free...}

00:12:33.710 --> 00:12:35.740
That's awful, Pops.

00:12:35.740 --> 00:12:38.150
Well, I'll let you off 
the hook for today.

00:12:38.150 --> 00:12:40.490
I'm in a good mood, so I'll 
tell you your fortune.

00:12:40.480 --> 00:12:42.110
<i>And to celebrate,</i>

00:12:42.110 --> 00:12:45.160
<i>I'm supposed to go drinking 
with Honda tonight.</i>

00:12:45.550 --> 00:12:47.750
Say hello to Uncle Honda for me.

00:12:47.750 --> 00:12:50.320
Make sure you don't 
drink too much— Hm?

00:12:50.320 --> 00:12:51.410
What's wrong?

00:12:52.250 --> 00:12:53.980
There'll be trouble today.

00:12:53.980 --> 00:12:57.510
It's necessary to put interactions 
with customers first today.

00:12:58.260 --> 00:13:00.550
Well, since it's you, Pops, 
everything should be fine.

00:13:01.470 --> 00:13:02.750
Of course!

00:13:02.750 --> 00:13:05.360
Customers are number 
one at Sancho Panza!

00:13:05.360 --> 00:13:07.050
Thanks, Ginka.

00:13:08.970 --> 00:13:11.270
<i>It has been two weeks 
since all the employees</i>

00:13:11.270 --> 00:13:14.690
<i>of the money lending company 
suddenly disappeared.</i>

00:13:13.560 --> 00:13:18.560
All Employees From a Money Lending Company Mysteriously Disappeared?!

00:13:14.690 --> 00:13:16.350
<i>There have still been no leads,</i>

00:13:16.350 --> 00:13:18.560
<i>but police are assuming there was 
some kind of trouble.</i>

00:13:23.860 --> 00:13:25.990
See? It's like I told you, right?

00:13:30.980 --> 00:13:33.310
Today's the day to make or break it.

00:13:37.500 --> 00:13:40.420
I want to hurry and go in.

00:13:44.010 --> 00:13:48.760
How you sift the flour is 
important in making cakes.

00:13:48.760 --> 00:13:52.890
The results of the physical 
indicate that Akari-oneetan

00:13:53.430 --> 00:13:57.800
has a stronger emotional pulse flowing 
through her than most people.

00:13:57.800 --> 00:13:59.190
People!

00:14:00.090 --> 00:14:01.820
What does that mean?

00:14:02.380 --> 00:14:04.330
When you enter the Astralux,

00:14:04.330 --> 00:14:06.530
your thoughts materialize a lot more.

00:14:06.830 --> 00:14:09.620
So when anyone touches you,

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:13.620
your thoughts are transferred, 
and they can hear voices.

00:14:14.910 --> 00:14:17.870
I sort of get it, but I don't.

00:14:17.860 --> 00:14:19.120
What?

00:14:19.780 --> 00:14:21.830
I can hear Akari's voice.

00:14:21.830 --> 00:14:25.620
It's saying, "Aw, I want 
to skip class and go home."

00:14:25.630 --> 00:14:28.680
What? That's not what I'm thinking.

00:14:29.630 --> 00:14:35.500
Luna's thinking, "Don't touch 
Akari-san!" Wow, scary.

00:14:35.500 --> 00:14:37.020
Th-That's not...

00:14:37.950 --> 00:14:39.170
For crying out loud...

00:14:40.940 --> 00:14:43.320
What? A customer got burned?

00:14:43.720 --> 00:14:44.810
Where?

00:14:44.810 --> 00:14:45.860
Within the city.

00:14:45.860 --> 00:14:46.870
All right,

00:14:47.550 --> 00:14:48.610
bring the car around.

00:14:48.970 --> 00:14:52.120
But don't you have dinner 
with Honda-sama today?

00:14:52.410 --> 00:14:56.290
Customers come first. That's 
what Honda taught me.

00:14:58.100 --> 00:15:01.000
But you really did a great 
job turning things around.

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:04.550
You must really have some luck 
when it comes to business.

00:15:04.700 --> 00:15:07.210
To think that all of the 
loan sharks disappeared...

00:15:07.210 --> 00:15:10.380
No kidding. Talk about 
mysterious things happening.

00:15:10.400 --> 00:15:12.930
Did you use some sort 
of magic, Honda-san?

00:15:14.080 --> 00:15:16.930
Oh, it's rather simple.

00:15:19.220 --> 00:15:22.310
It just involves making a little trade.

00:15:35.280 --> 00:15:37.910
Tell me your desires.

00:15:38.440 --> 00:15:40.830
Thank you so much for coming.

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:44.590
It wasn't even that bad, 
and for the president to come...

00:15:44.580 --> 00:15:47.840
I'm totally your fan now.

00:15:48.120 --> 00:15:49.910
Thank you very much.

00:15:49.910 --> 00:15:53.190
Please keep using our 
products in the future.

00:15:54.690 --> 00:15:57.060
Thank goodness she was 
a great customer.

00:15:57.060 --> 00:15:58.070
I will drive you, sir.

00:15:58.060 --> 00:15:59.810
Don't worry about it. I'll take a taxi.

00:15:59.830 --> 00:16:02.650
I'm going to head to Honda's. 
See you tomorrow.

00:16:07.000 --> 00:16:08.300
Yataro.

00:16:10.750 --> 00:16:12.420
Hey, Honda.

00:16:12.420 --> 00:16:13.780
Why are you here?

00:16:16.120 --> 00:16:17.370
Who's that?

00:16:18.030 --> 00:16:19.530
Not him.

00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:21.800
I smell bad blood from him.

00:16:24.200 --> 00:16:25.130
Honda?

00:16:25.640 --> 00:16:26.670
Kill him.

00:16:32.020 --> 00:16:32.590
That's...

00:16:34.710 --> 00:16:36.760
Don't tell me you've 
turned into a Daemonia!

00:16:37.870 --> 00:16:39.770
I don't want him to live.

00:16:40.310 --> 00:16:43.560
He's got the blood of 
Elemental Tarot users.

00:16:54.490 --> 00:16:56.320
The talisman of Temperance?

00:17:05.830 --> 00:17:08.710
Honda... Why?

00:17:40.130 --> 00:17:42.110
Stop! Stop it!

00:17:43.940 --> 00:17:45.040
Honda!

00:17:54.080 --> 00:17:55.170
Pops!

00:17:55.850 --> 00:17:58.930
It can't be... Uncle Honda?

00:18:11.650 --> 00:18:13.710
Akari, do you understand it?

00:18:18.450 --> 00:18:21.780
Is that you, Ginka-chan?

00:18:23.090 --> 00:18:24.290
Uncle...

00:18:24.580 --> 00:18:28.290
I haven't seen you in a while 
and you've grown so much.

00:18:29.120 --> 00:18:30.290
Why?

00:18:31.130 --> 00:18:33.380
Why'd you turn into a Daemonia?

00:18:33.750 --> 00:18:38.300
Sorry, my heart was weak.

00:18:38.970 --> 00:18:42.510
Now I... Yataro and Ginka-chan...

00:18:48.440 --> 00:18:49.730
I'm sorry.

00:18:50.270 --> 00:18:57.150
I can't control my 
own body anymore.

00:18:58.810 --> 00:18:59.820
Uncle!

00:19:01.810 --> 00:19:02.370
Ginka!

00:19:05.240 --> 00:19:11.250
I thought of you 
as my own daughter...

00:19:13.430 --> 00:19:14.590
Ginka...

00:19:22.220 --> 00:19:24.600
This is the result of 
being able to hear his voice.

00:19:24.890 --> 00:19:28.100
If you hadn't heard it, you 
could have fought without hesitation.

00:19:28.460 --> 00:19:30.080
Seira, wait! That person is—

00:19:30.080 --> 00:19:31.880
It's just like Seira said.

00:19:33.780 --> 00:19:35.360
If I couldn't hear him...

00:19:36.530 --> 00:19:39.860
If I didn't know, I wouldn't suffer.

00:19:40.570 --> 00:19:42.200
But Uncle

00:19:43.070 --> 00:19:44.370
is worse off.

00:19:47.790 --> 00:19:48.700
I'm

00:19:49.620 --> 00:19:51.120
going to let Uncle rest in peace!

00:20:24.570 --> 00:20:27.200
<i>It's about time to flip us over!</i>

00:20:27.490 --> 00:20:29.750
Okay! Gimme a sec!

00:20:36.600 --> 00:20:39.210
Hey, Akari. What's wrong?

00:20:41.550 --> 00:20:43.970
I'm guessing you came because 
you were worried about me.

00:20:45.430 --> 00:20:48.430
Because you heard his voice...

00:20:48.430 --> 00:20:50.810
I'm the one that took your hand.

00:20:50.830 --> 00:20:54.760
I wanted to talk to Uncle. 
That's all that was.

00:20:55.900 --> 00:20:58.110
<i>It's about ready!</i>

00:20:58.130 --> 00:20:59.980
You'll have some takoyaki, right?

00:21:01.860 --> 00:21:05.320
Pops lost all memory of Honda-san.

00:21:06.250 --> 00:21:07.120
I see...

00:21:07.640 --> 00:21:11.080
So I'm the only one 
that remembers Uncle.

00:21:11.380 --> 00:21:14.620
I'm also the only one that 
heard his last words.

00:21:17.740 --> 00:21:20.850
I had thought that exterminating 
the Daemonia was somehow

00:21:20.850 --> 00:21:24.440
happening on some world that 
had nothing to do with me.

00:21:25.410 --> 00:21:28.520
I mean, I exterminate 
them and get money.

00:21:28.520 --> 00:21:32.080
I thought it didn't matter 
who the Daemonia was.

00:21:33.420 --> 00:21:36.560
Just like Pops said, it's a 
job fighting for justice.

00:21:38.970 --> 00:21:41.620
It's true that it might 
have been easier if

00:21:41.610 --> 00:21:43.280
I hadn't heard his voice.

00:21:43.820 --> 00:21:45.030
But,

00:21:45.040 --> 00:21:48.780
I think I understand why you're 
so concerned about this now.

00:21:50.620 --> 00:21:54.330
If it was my Pops in the 
place of Uncle Honda,

00:21:54.330 --> 00:21:57.420
would he have lost to temptation?

00:21:58.760 --> 00:22:01.240
If things had been a little different...

00:22:01.710 --> 00:22:03.960
Pops and I...

00:23:26.380 --> 00:23:33.240
<b>The image of a woman pouring water, 
the blessing of nature, onto the land, 
and the image of stars shining in the sky, 
represents hopes and promises for the 
future, as well as a bright future and possibilities.</b>

00:23:26.380 --> 00:23:41.990
<b>#17  The Star</b>

00:23:27.330 --> 00:23:29.720
Heyo, the two of us make 
up Lapschrö, meow.

00:23:29.720 --> 00:23:31.690
You don't take anything 
seriously! We are familiars.

00:23:31.690 --> 00:23:32.620
You need to acknowledge that.

00:23:32.620 --> 00:23:34.810
It's our job as familiars 
to communicate, meow.

00:23:33.240 --> 00:23:34.910
<b>The Star card is a very positive card 
that shows the arrival of possible chances 
and changes in the future.</b>

00:23:34.810 --> 00:23:36.890
Since you don't want to 
communicate the explanation

00:23:34.910 --> 00:23:37.740
<b>If you choose this card, changes could occur 
in your situation, like the light shining upon you, and the path to making your hopes 
come true may become apparent.</b>

00:23:36.890 --> 00:23:38.230
on the cards, you fail as a familiar, meow.

00:23:37.740 --> 00:23:41.770
<b>If reversed, what would have been a good 
situation or bright possibilities or hopes 
will instead show that you may have lost faith 
in yourself, you may be thinking too much, 
become emotional, or have become negative.</b>

00:23:37.890 --> 00:24:39.190
<b>To the Ends with the Star</b>

00:23:38.230 --> 00:23:39.150
A valid argument.

00:23:39.150 --> 00:23:41.700
See you next time!
